{{- /*
  Windows Terminal "fragment extension" — a native, documented mechanism
  (https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/terminal/json-fragment-extensions) for third parties to
  contribute profiles/color schemes WITHOUT touching the user's real settings.json. Works
  regardless of whether Windows Terminal is packaged (winget/Store) or not, since this path is
  the generic third-party drop location, not Windows Terminal's own config file.

  Deliberately does NOT set defaultProfile or any other global setting (fragments can't — only
  settings.json can, and that file's location is fragile for MSIX/winget installs plus is real
  JSONC the user may have hand-edited, see CONCEPT_ROADMAP.md §7 for why that's out of scope).
  Own, fixed GUID below (never reused/regenerated) so this is always additive, never an
  `"updates"` reference to an existing profile — no possible collision with the user's real data.

  font.face added 2026-08-17 (jetbrains-mono-nerd-font in packages.yaml) — needed for the
  Oh My Posh prompt's segment glyphs to render instead of tofu boxes, confirmed live on
  winlab.local. "JetBrainsMono NF" is the Windows-specific family name (DEVCOM's WiX build),
  NOT "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font" like the Homebrew cask used for Ghostty on macOS.
*/ -}}
{
    "profiles": [
        {
            "guid": "{1ae1727f-65b8-4645-b6d2-ee9d98d5c1d1}",
            "name": "Dotfiles",
            "commandline": "pwsh.exe -NoLogo",
            "font": {
                "face": "JetBrainsMono NF",
                "size": {{ if eq .deployment.profile "work" }}14{{ else }}13{{ end }}
            }
        }
    ]
}
